# Chinese Audio Practice Generator

## Project Overview

A Python web app that generates MP3 audio files of Chinese dialogue conversations
using edge-tts, with different male/female voices per speaker. Built for a beginner
Mandarin learner (lessons 1-5).

## How to Run

```bash
# Activate virtual environment
source venv/bin/activate

# Web UI (paste and generate)
python app.py
# Opens http://localhost:5000
```

## Project Structure

- `app.py` — Flask web server (main entry point for web UI)
- `tts_engine.py` — Core TTS logic: parse_dialogue, detect_speakers, generate_audio
- `conversation_library.py` — 45 items for the web UI random-shuffle library (32 full dialogues + 10 short dialogues + 5 single-speaker texts)
- `templates/index.html` — Web UI (single page, loads a random conversation on each visit)
- `templates/login.html` — Passcode page, used only when `APP_PASSCODE` is set
- `gunicorn.conf.py` — Production server settings shared by Render and Docker
- `render.yaml` — Render deployment config (Blueprint spec)
- `Dockerfile` — Hugging Face Spaces (Docker SDK) deployment
- `requirements.txt` — edge-tts, flask, gunicorn, pypinyin
- `venv/` — Python virtual environment

## Deployment

The app is deployed on Render (free tier).

- **Live URL**: https://chinese-dialogue-audio.onrender.com/
- **Config**: `render.yaml` (Blueprint spec — auto-detected by Render)
- **WSGI server**: gunicorn (`gunicorn app:app`, settings in `gunicorn.conf.py`)
- **Hugging Face Spaces**: `Dockerfile` plus the README front matter (`sdk: docker`, port 7860)
- **Passcode**: optional `APP_PASSCODE` env var gates every route except `/login` and `/healthz`
- **Auto-deploy**: Pushes to the main branch on GitHub trigger a redeploy
- **Cold starts**: Free tier spins down after 15 min of inactivity; first request takes ~30s

## Paste Format for Web UI

```
售货员：您好！您要什么？
顾客：我要两件T恤。
```

Both Chinese colon (：) and ASCII colon (:) are supported.

## Web UI Features

- **Show Pinyin**: Toggle button overlays pinyin with tone marks above each Chinese character inline in the text panel. Applies tone sandhi rules (3rd+3rd, 一, 不) and highlights changed tones in amber.
- **Highlight Words**: Toggle button (enabled after audio generation) highlights the currently-spoken character during audio playback. Word-level timing from edge-tts WordBoundary events is interpolated to per-character timing. Works independently or combined with Show Pinyin — the overlay mimics the textarea (monospace, same border) or pinyin overlay (sans-serif, accent border, ruby annotations) so toggling highlight on/off causes no visual change except the moving highlight itself. The active character gets a subtle semi-transparent red background (`hw-active` class, `rgba(255, 90, 90, 0.35)`). Auto-scrolls to keep the highlighted character visible.
- **Click-to-Edit**: When pinyin or highlight overlay is active, clicking on the overlay (without selecting text) or pressing any key dismisses the overlay and focuses the editable textarea. A subtle hover hint ("click here or start typing to edit") appears on active overlays. The textarea itself is always editable — users can clear the random conversation and type/paste their own dialogue text.
- **Select-to-Translate**: Select any word(s) in the textarea, pinyin overlay, or highlight overlay to see an instant English translation tooltip. Pinyin annotations are stripped so only characters are sent for translation. The page calls Google's unofficial `translate_a/single` endpoint directly from the browser (allowed by the CSP `connect-src`); there is no server-side translate route, because Google blocks that endpoint from Render's IPs.
- **Voice Assignment**: Auto-detects speakers and lets you pick male/female voices for each.
- **Speed Slider**: Adjust speech rate from -50% to +50%.
- **Random Conversation Library**: Each page load shows a random conversation from a library of 45 items (32 full dialogues + 10 short dialogues + 5 single-speaker texts at easy/medium/hard difficulty). A small "Shuffle" button next to the "Dialogue Text" heading loads a new random conversation without a full page reload. Library data lives in `conversation_library.py`; served via `GET /random-conversation` endpoint.

## Audio Generation Architecture

The `/generate` endpoint returns JSON `{ audio, timing }`: `audio` is the base64-encoded MP3, which the page turns into a Blob URL for playback and download, so the server keeps no state. The `timing` array contains per-line objects with word-level `start`/`end` times (seconds) relative to the combined audio, computed from edge-tts `WordBoundary` events (requires `boundary="WordBoundary"` kwarg) plus segment durations and the fixed pause between lines.

Lines are synthesized concurrently (up to 5 at once) with retries. edge-tts always returns constant-bitrate MP3 (24 kHz, 48 kbps, mono), so a segment's duration is `len(bytes) / 6000` and segments are joined by byte concatenation with pre-built silent frames between them. No ffmpeg is used.

`generate_audio()` in `tts_engine.py` returns `(mp3_bytes, timing)`.

## Available Voices

- zh-CN-XiaoxiaoNeural — female, natural (default for 1st speaker)
- zh-CN-XiaoyiNeural — female, young
- zh-CN-YunxiNeural — male, natural (default for 2nd speaker)
- zh-CN-YunyangNeural — male, broadcast (default for narrator/旁白)
- zh-CN-YunjianNeural — male, sporty
- zh-CN-YunxiaNeural — male, boyish

## Complete Vocabulary Reference (Lessons 1-5)

### Numbers
零-十, 十一-九十九, 一百-九百九十九 (with 零 rule: 一百零二)

### Measure Words
瓶 (bottle), 盒 (box), 听 (can), 个 (general), 双 (pair), 件 (clothing), 顶 (hat), 块 (bar), 条 (pants)

### Money
块/元 (yuan), 毛 (0.1 yuan), 分 (0.01 yuan)

### Verbs
买, 要, 给, 找, 是

### Pronouns
我, 你, 您, 他, 她, 它 + 们

### Demonstratives
这/那 + MW + noun; 这个, 那个

### People
售货员, 顾客, 师傅

### Greetings
你好, 您好, 你好吗, 我很好, 你呢, 晚安, 再见, 谢谢, 生日快乐

### Shopping Phrases
多少钱, 一共, 还要别的吗, 不要了, 扫码还是现金, 现金

### Food/Drink
可乐, 牛奶, 水, 矿泉水, 三明治, 面包, 鸡蛋, 巧克力, 方便面, 水果, 冰棍, 鸡肉, 牛肉

### Clothing
鞋, T恤, 帽子, 裤子, 袜子

### Toiletries
肥皂, 纸巾, 牙刷, 洗发水, 浴液, 毛巾

### Other Nouns
礼物, 钱, 汽油, 东西

### Currencies
美元, 欧元, 日元, 韩币, 泰铢

### Adverbs/Adjectives
很, 好, 经常, 大一点儿, 小一点儿

### Sentence Patterns
我要买..., X多少钱？, 一共...钱, 给您..., 找您..., 我经常买..., 这是..., 我是...
